  "term": "kuru",
  "definition": "Kuru is a rare prion disease that occurred among the Fore people of the New Guinea highlands, especially in adult women and children. It causes a gradual onset of shaking and loss of coordination, followed by worsening weakness and loss of bladder control, and is linked to ritual cannibalism.",
